{"chunk":"No provision of this Code shall affect any structure or use for which a building or\n               use permit is lawfully issued prior to the effective date of this code, as amended;\n               provided, that construction work under such building permit, or occupancy under such\n               use permit, is commenced within six months of the date of such permit and proceeds\n               in good faith continuously so far as is reasonably practical under the circumstances;\n               and provided further that all construction work is completed within two years from\n               the effective date of this code and in accordance with the building permit as in effect\n               on said effective date. A Proposed Project, however, shall be exempt from the provisions of an amendment to\n               this Code, if application to the Inspectional Services Department for a building or\n               use permit has been made prior to the first notice of hearing before the Zoning Commission\n               for adoption of an amendment, and (1) no Zoning Relief is required, or (2) any required\n               Zoning Relief has been or thereafter is granted by the Board of Appeal; provided that\n               construction work under such building permit, or occupancy under such occupancy permit,\n               as the case may be, is commenced within six (6) months of the date of such permit\n               issue and proceeds in good faith continuously so far as is reasonably practicable\n               under the circumstances. (Text Amd.","document":"ARTICLE_4_-_APPLICATION_OF_REGULATIONS","city":"boston","heading_1":"ARTICLE 4 APPLICATION OF REGULATIONS","heading_2":"Section 4-2. Structure or Use Approved Prior to Effective Date of Code.","url":"https:\/\/library.municode.com\/MA\/Boston\/codes\/Redevelopment_Authority?nodeId=ART4APRE_S4-2STUSAPPREFDACO","district_code":[],"district_category":[],"embedding":[-0.0204673987,-0.0347199477,-0.00